'''Loki Beaker''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|l|oʊ|k|i|_|ˈ|b|i:|k|ə|r}}) is a pre-made playable [[Sim]] residing in [[Strangetown]] in ''[[The Sims 2]]'' for [[The Sims 2|PC]] and [[The Sims 2 (PSP)|PSP]], and formerly in [[Aurora Skies]], one of the [[world]]s available for purchase from ''[[TheSims3.com#The Sims 3 Store|The Sims 3 Store]]''. He is [[marriage|married]] to [[Circe Beaker|Circe]]. He has a younger sister, [[Erin Singles|Erin]], and is the son of [[Bjorn Beaker|Bjorn]] and [[Gundrun Beaker|Gundrun]]. He has blond hair and dark blue eyes.<ref>In ''[[The Sims 2]]'' for [[The Sims 2 (PSP)|PSP]], his eyes are brown.</ref> He is portrayed as a mad scientist. His surname is a play on a laboratory container with a pouring lip.

Loki genetically engineered [[Atom Beaker]] and [[Ceres Beaker]], who appear in ''[[The Sims 3: Into the Future]]''. He appears with them as well as [[Beaker family|his family]] from ''The Sims 2'' in the ''[[The Sims 4]]'' [[Gallery]].

==Biography==
===Life leading in The Sims 3===
In ''[[The Sims 3]]'', Loki reappears as a [[child]], living with [[Gundrun Beaker|his mother]], [[Bjorn Beaker|father]], and [[Erin Singles|younger sister]] in [[Aurora Skies]]. His overall [[personality]] as a child is much less serious and sinister than his [[adult]] counterpart in ''[[The Sims 2]]'', implying a significant change in personality later in his life. He has seven [[skill]] points in the [[Kingdomino Table|Dominoes]] [[secret skill]], if ''[[The Sims 3: Showtime]]'' is installed. However, in ''The Sims 2'', he has low [[Creativity (skill)|creativity]], which is connected to [[Writing (The Sims 3)|writing]]. When the family is first played, Loki is 4 days away from becoming a [[teen]]. He carries a [[computer|laptop]], a randomly generated [[book]], and a [[toy]] in his [[inventory]].

===Life leading in The Sims 2===
Loki lives in [[Strangetown]] with his wife, [[Circe Beaker|Circe]]. He wears a blue sweater, dark gray jeans, and black shoes. He provides a home for [[Nervous Subject]], whom he and his wife, Circe, use as a subject for cruel [[Science (hobby)|science]] experiments. When first played, he is 20 days away from becoming an [[elder]]. Loki is [[voice]]d by Dave Boat.

As a [[teen]]ager, he was excellent in [[school]] and lost a [[Fighting|fight]] with [[General Buzz Grunt]]. Loki has a job in the [[Science]] [[career]] as an Inventor (Level 6). He is enemies with [[Pascal Curious]] and considered an enemy by [[Vidcund Curious]], who are two of the three [[Curious family|Curious]] brothers. The rivalry started when they were all teenagers. Vidcund was Circe's first flame, and in a storytelling picture, Loki and Pascal got into a fight. Though neither of them has any [[memories|memory]] of it, it is presumed that Loki won.

It is suggested that he and his sister have Scandinavian, perhaps Icelandic, ancestry, due to their last name and [[Aurora Skies]] strongly resembling Iceland. Because the [[1 Tesla Court|Beaker household]] already has [[Aspiration reward (The Sims 2)|aspiration]] and [[career rewards]] lying around on the first floor, as well as Loki being seen testing the [[Eclectic and Enigmatic Energizer]] on Nervous in the storybook image, it is conceivable that Loki invented some of the [[Aspiration (The Sims 2)|aspiration]] and career rewards.

Strangely, Loki has memories of his sister [[Erin Singles|Erin]] growing up well, even though Erin has no memories of Loki. Also, Erin has not noticed that Loki got [[marriage|married]], and she does not know Circe. Despite being a [[Knowledge]] [[Sim]], Loki will usually have a [[wants and fears|fear]] of seeing a [[ghost]] when [[Beaker family|the family]] is first played. Because he has reached level 6 of the Science career, Loki has a [[Career rewards#Science|Science career reward]] available for him to purchase, disregarding the fact that there is already one inside the house. 

When the lot is loaded for the first time and [[free will]] is enabled, there is a high chance that Loki will [[autonomous reaction|autonomously]] attempt to gossip with Nervous, in which case Nervous will always reject the [[interaction]].

Loki, as well as his wife, possesses corrupt [[relationship]] data found in [[Package editor|SimPE]], implying unknown family relations to several members of the [[Curious family]] and the [[Grunt family]], namely Pascal, Vidcund, [[Kitty Curious|Kitty]], and [[Annie Hogleg|Annie]] and [[Hamm Hogleg]], as well as General Buzz Grunt and his grandmother, [[Mary Melons]]. Oddly enough, Loki's relationship data towards Mary considers her an enemy, despite being an ancestral Sim Loki couldn't have met.

Very fittingly, along with his wife, Loki's pre-destined [[hobby]] will be [[Science (hobby)|Science]], because of his very neat and serious personality, if ''[[The Sims 2: FreeTime|FreeTime]]'' is installed. Strangely, if Loki's appearance is [[Game guide:How to extract the appearance of in-game Sims#The Sims 2|extracted]] with SimPE to [[Body Shop]], he will be [[Fitness (attribute)|thin]] instead of fit. The reason for this is that he has the fitness texture for thin Sims instead of the one for fit Sims.

This implies that he was originally thin, and his fitness level was subsequently modified with a program like SimPE. The only way for him to have the fitness texture for fit Sims without [[mod|hacks]] is by having him overeat until he becomes thin, and then have him work out until he is fit again. This also happens with many other pre-made Sims in ''The Sims 2''.
<blockquote class="note">In Norse mythology, Loki is the Norse god of [[fire]] and mischief, destined to break free of his prison and join the giants in Ragnarok, the world-ending battle.</blockquote>

===Life leading in The Sims 2 (PSP)===
Loki appears as a mad scientist who had kidnapped [[Gimi Branko]] for tests, since his previous guinea pig, [[Nervous Subject]], [[death|died]] after getting instructed by Loki to use one of the instruments, likely an [[Aspiration reward (The Sims 2)|aspiration reward]], at a too low [[Aspiration bar|aspiration level]], according to [[Emily Emory]]. This is a reference to the negative side effects possibly occurring when directing a [[Sim]] to use such a reward at below gold level in ''[[The Sims 2]]''.

He also finds out his wife, [[Circe Beaker|Circe]], was having an [[affair]] with [[Dominic Newlow]].

Loki's brow is different in the [[The Sims 2 (PSP)|PSP version]], simply due to the limitations of the [[Create a Sim|Create-A-Sim]] menu. It looks fairly normal and doesn't cover his eyes as much. Also, he wears blue jeans instead of dark gray.

According to the game's data, he's [[interest]]ed in School, Entertainment, and, in contrast to his PC counterpart, Weather and Health.

Loki's secrets in ''The Sims 2 (PSP)'':
*[[File:Personal.png|30x30px]]'''(Personal):''' Loves to chew on aluminum foil to make his teeth "buzz".
*[[File:Intimate.png|30x30px]]'''(Intimate):''' That thick, wavy hair is really just a high-tech evil-genius toupee.
*[[File:Dark.png|30x30px]]'''(Dark):''' Met his wife by lurking in an online chatroom devoted to lurking in online chatrooms.
*[[File:Secret.png|30x30px]]'''(Loki's Secret Patents):''' Loki has secret patents for an electric vomit recycler and fuzzy carrying case. Sounds delicious!

===Life leading to The Sims 4===
An official [[Maxis]] recreation of Loki and [[Beaker family|his family]] was uploaded to [[Gallery|''The Sims 4'' Gallery]] on March 14, 2019, marking the 19th anniversary of ''[[The Sims]]''.<ref>[https://www.ea.com/games/the-sims/the-sims-4/gallery/item/DvqXGEaNEemHKnldy2Ruvw The Beaker Family by Maxis]</ref> In this [[Alternate universe|timeline]], he lives with his wife, [[Circe Beaker|Circe]], and [[Nervous Subject]], like in ''[[The Sims 2]]'', but also with his [[child]]ren, [[Atom Beaker|Atom]] and [[Ceres Beaker|Ceres]]. Atom and Ceres had first appeared as [[adult]]s in [[Oasis Landing]], the [[Sub-neighborhood|sub-world]] shipped with ''[[The Sims 3: Into the Future]]'', alongside their [[Plumbot]] friend [[Cyclotron]]. Their [[biography|biographies]] described them as twins who were [[genetics|genetically]] engineered by Loki. In this recreation, they are children wearing [[alien]] suits from ''[[The Sims 4: Get to Work]]''. The twins view Loki as their father, but only recognize Circe as their stepmother. Cyclotron does not appear in this version of the household.

